  "title": "Exponential Algorithms for Knapsack",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture\n\nThe famous 0-1 Knapsack problem is: Given $a_{1},a_{2},\\dots,a_{n}$ and $b$ integers, determine whether or not there are $0-1$ values $x_{1},x_{2},\\dots,x_{n}$ so that $$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} a_{i}x_{i} = b.$$The best known worst-case algorithm runs in time$2^{n/2}$times a polynomial in$n$. Is there an algorithm that runs in time$2^{n/3}$?",
